  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Develop and evaluate an integrated data-curation strategy and the Medical Multimodal Multitask Foundation Model (M3FM) for scalable lung-cancer screening across multiscale 3D LDCT scans, heterogeneous clinical data, and multiple LCS workflow tasks.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When LCS has clinically important mortality impact but existing workflows, data curation, annotation, and 3D-CT modeling constraints limit current approaches, the paper-level response is to develop and evaluate an integrated, scalable multimodal multitask LCS framework."];
  "R1" [label="(0,0,0) Given that AI promises to improve the quality and efficiency of lung cancer screening, AI is a plausible tool for helping address key LCS implementation challenges."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) The multimodal, multitask nature of the LCS setting addressed by this work makes a foundation-model approach a plausible direction for LCS AI."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Because this LCS work involves aligning high-dimensional images with other clinical datasets across many screening tasks, a foundation-model paradigm is a plausible solution direction."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) An effective LCS foundation-model solution should address both scalable data curation and model-architecture or compute constraints for volumetric 3D CT."];
